<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Stanbic half yr EPS, div rise.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Stanbic half yr EPS, div rise.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended June 30</p>
<p>		    (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)	 693.0	   vs 602.0</p>
<p>    Attrib shr (cts)	   700.0	   vs 575.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    136.0	   vs 109.0</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast headline earnings rising to between 688.0 and 725.0 cents with consensus at 704.3. They expected the dividend in a range of 127.5-132.0 cents, averaging out at 130.0 cents.</p>
<p>    Net income		   842.0	   vs 690.0</p>
<p>    Net interest income	1,819.0	 vs 1,868.0</p>
<p>    Non-interest income	2,003.0	 vs 1,450.0</p>
<p>    Credit loss provision    534.0	   vs 288.0</p>
<p>    Operating profit	   962.0	   vs 867.0</p>
<p>    Tax			    250.0	   vs 255.0</p>
<p>Div payable Sept 19</p>
<p>On register August 22</p>
<p>Full name: Standard Bank Investment Corp Ltd (Stanbic)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  8.0 gain	vs 32.ooss</p>
<p>NOTE - The substantial increase in provision was mainly in respect of the full anticipated exposure to Pepsi bottler New Age Beverages and the higher provisioning required on instalment sale debtors.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
